From: Fred Horch <fred.horch@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:37:54 -0400
Subject: Add in-window close button to top-right corner

Files (Nautilus) and other client-decorated windows provide a close button,
but Omawrite had no titlebar or window close button, forcing the user to
rely on Super+W keyboard shortcut to close the window.

This patch adds WindowCloseButton.qml to the top right of Omawrite,
styled with a subtle circular disc matching Omarchy/Files app aesthetics,
connected to win.close() which safely prompts on unsaved changes.

Retires when: Omawrite upstream ships a native close button in pkgver > 0.5.0

(Patch carried in ~/pkgs by Fred's Omarchy workstation; registry: https://github.com/greenermoose/omarchy-fred-ecosystem)

AI-Tool: claude 2.1.274
AI-Model: Claude Opus 5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
